, 21, 8, 400, 374, 17779, 553, 220, 22, 374, 3070, 18, 334, 13, 151645], "output_tokens": 385, "input_tokens": 53, "capped": false, "completion": "We are given that:\n\n$$\nn \\equiv 2 \\pmod{7}\n$$\n\nWe are asked to find the remainder when:\n\n$$\n(n + 2)(n + 4)(n + 6)\n$$\n\nis divided by 7.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Use the given congruence\n\nSince $ n \\equiv 2 \\pmod{7} $, we can substitute $ n = 2 $ into the expression modulo 7:\n\n$$\n(n + 2)(n + 4)(n + 6) \\equiv (2 + 2)(2 + 4)(2 + 6) \\pmod{7}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\equiv (4)(6)(8) \\pmod{7}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Simplify each term modulo 7\n\n- $ 4 \\equiv 4 \\pmod{7} $\n- $ 6 \\equiv 6 \\pmod{7} $\n- $ 8 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{7} $ (since $ 8 - 7 = 1 $)\n\nSo the expression becomes:\n\n$$\n(4)(6)(1) \\pmod{7}\n$$\n\n$$\n= 4 \\cdot 6 \\cdot 1 = 24 \\pmod{7}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Simplify $ 24 \\mod 7 $\n\n$$\n24 \\div 7 = 3 \\text{ remainder } 3\n$$\n\nSo:\n\n$$\n24 \\equiv 3 \\pmod{7}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### \u2705 Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{3}\n$$\n\nSo, the remainder when $ (n + 2)(n + 4)(n + 6) $ is divided by 7 is **3**.", "diagnostic_seconds": 10.14818869298324}
